WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:05.930
Speaker 1: So we talked about should unvaccinated
workers be fired?

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:11.320
And my position there is if the company has
announced you must be vaccinated or you can't

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:16.330
work here, they cannot be empty threats that
if you're saying you're going to fire people,

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:19.150
if they're not vaccinated, you've absolutely
got to do it.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:25.500
OK, so the next question is when people when
workers say I'll quit.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.900
Do they actually do it and increasingly the
evidence is they do not.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.280
Let's look at a couple articles from Massachusetts
related to Massachusetts state police.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:39.000
There are reportedly just under twenty two
hundred state troopers right now.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.880
OK, let's call it two hundred.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.550
It's actually twenty one eighty seven.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:49.899
Dozens of Massachusetts state police troopers
have been resigning, a claim that they are

00:00:49.899 --> 00:00:52.329
resigning over the covid vaccine mandate.

00:00:52.329 --> 00:00:56.790
Union says this is an article from yesterday
and this article says the State Police Association

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:01.390
of Massachusetts says dozens of troopers have
submitted their resignation papers as a result

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:02.579
of the mandate.

00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:06.639
The state is requiring all executive department
employees to show proof of vaccination by

00:01:06.639 --> 00:01:09.219
the 17th or risk losing their jobs.

00:01:09.219 --> 00:01:13.679
About 20 percent of state police employees
are not vaccinated, according to the union's

00:01:13.679 --> 00:01:18.240
attorney, a source told ABC TV on Monday.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:25.499
Only one state trooper has told human resources
they would resign because of the vaccine mandate.

00:01:25.499 --> 00:01:29.960
They also said there are others who spoke
with H.R. to evaluate what their pensions

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:33.939
would be if they chose to retire.

00:01:33.939 --> 00:01:39.219
The union released this statement to date,
dozens of troopers have submitted resignation

00:01:39.219 --> 00:01:46.069
paperwork, some of whom planned to retire
to to other departments offering alternatives

00:01:46.069 --> 00:01:49.039
such as mask wearing and regular testing.

00:01:49.039 --> 00:01:54.109
The state police are already critically short
staffed and acknowledged this by the unprecedented

00:01:54.109 --> 00:01:57.810
moves which took troopers from specialty units
that investigate homicides.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:04.869
So you've got a story, which is the union
says dozens have submitted resignation paperwork,

00:02:04.869 --> 00:02:10.680
but then only one person has actually said,
I'm resigning to human resources.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:15.650
Another article from the Boston Globe State
Police Union says dozens of troopers plan

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:22.130
to resign due to vaccine mandate, but police
spokesman says only one definitively has.

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:28.900
So we have to wonder we have to wonder is
what's going on with the union?

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:33.280
The union claiming dozens have submitted resignation.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:38.380
Does that actually translate to people are
actually really going to quit?

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:44.190
So far, it's one out of two thousand one hundred
and eighty seven Massachusetts state troopers

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:47.650
that have actually communicated this to human
resources.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:54.720
I'm not saying that the union is lying, but
I'm wondering whether they've collected resignation

00:02:54.720 --> 00:03:00.970
letters that many don't actually intend to
give to anybody in human resources as part

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:03.700
of a political statement of sorts.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:08.430
These are good jobs, you know, but there's
the waiting list.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:12.350
To become a Massachusetts state trooper is
very, very long.

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:14.250
And these are really good jobs.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:18.920
Are they really going to quit over a vaccine
requirement in particular when their pensions

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:20.440
may be at risk?

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:26.840
The real headline so far seems to be fewer
than what is it.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:32.900
One tenth of one percent of troopers have
actually resisted the vaccination requirement.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:37.040
It's very easy to talk about quitting a well-paying
job with great health care and retirement

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:39.750
benefits over a safe vaccine.

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:43.250
But it's a very different thing to actually
go and to do it.

00:03:43.250 --> 00:04:48.099
So my question is, are a lot of these people
just bluffing and they're not really going

00:04:48.099 --> 00:04:51.029
to quit?

